      "difficulty": "difficult",
      "evidence": "CDIAL 2245 lists the Shina bay- present and beṭu past together, while explicitly suggesting vasati for the present and warning of contamination and replacement by past-stem forms. The simplex bai imperatives do not resolve that historical analysis. Schmidt Gurezi byō̌nu to sit matches the full infinitive explicitly cited in 2245, but it likewise does not resolve the present-stem versus past-stem analysis. Schmidt Kohistani byō̌n and Astori biyō̌nu likewise preserve the full sitting stem without resolving the competing history. Rajapurohit byōno sit/stay also belongs to the present-stem comparison without resolving the alternative historical analysis.",
